# core/dependents-direct - Transitive dependents, via the direct predicate form.
#
# Answers: everything that reaches the focus element at any depth by following the
# predicates you named.
#
# Does NOT prove: impact, criticality or failure propagation - and not
# completeness either, because it follows only the predicates given. A dependency
# expressed through a relationship type you left out is silently absent.
#
# REQUIRES capabilities.direct_rel_triples. The converters emit direct
# source-predicate-target triples only with --emit-direct-rel-triples, which is
# off by default, so against ordinary converter output this template is refused
# rather than run. That refusal is the point: its predecessor made this the
# primary traversal route and returned zero rows on a default dataset.
#
# Never union these rows with core/neighbours-qualified. When direct triples are
# emitted, every relationship exists in both forms, so a union double-counts and
# nothing raises an error.
#
# PREDICATE_PATH is an alternation, capped, and required. Get the predicates from
# core/discover-relationship-types rather than assuming which ones this dataset
# uses; the notation ontologies are versioned in the namespace, so am: and am4:
# spell the same concept differently.
#
# Parameters: FOCUS_IRI, PREDICATE_PATH, LIMIT
{{PREFIXES}}
SELECT DISTINCT ?dependent ?dependentLabel
WHERE {
  {{GRAPH_OPEN:semantic}}
    VALUES ?focus { {{FOCUS_IRI}} }
    ?dependent ({{PREDICATE_PATH}})+ ?focus .
    FILTER(?dependent != ?focus)
    OPTIONAL { ?dependent {{PATH:label}} ?dependentLabel }
  {{GRAPH_CLOSE}}
}
ORDER BY ?dependentLabel ?dependent
LIMIT {{LIMIT}}
